From 7fcae69759225e666d5c984feb8bba95ae570a21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joaco2382 <104966815+Joaco2382@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:48:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: fragment varyings Wallpaper Engine shaders rely on

Wallpaper Engine compiles its GLSL shaders with HLSL rules, where vertex
outputs are one structure shared with the fragment stage and the fragment
inputs are parameters it can modify. Workshop shaders depend on both:

- a fragment shader can read a vertex varying it never declares
  (foliagesway.frag reads v_Bounds, workshop 2169779628): the missing
  declarations are added before main.
- a fragment shader can write to an input ("v_RefractTexCoord.xy = ...",
  workshop 2405891694): every varying it writes to gets a writable global
  copy filled from the input at the start of main, and a macro of the same
  name sends every use to the copy.

Parameter metadata with numbers written with leading zeros
("range":[0,01]) is also read now instead of losing the parameter's
default value.

Needs the glslang change that truncates mixed vector sizes in arithmetic
(src/External/glslang-WallpaperEngine) for the HlslShapes tests.

Tests: ShaderVaryings (3 more cases), HlslShapes (3 cases).
